WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.542 --> 00:00:02.000
CARTER MORGAN:
Today, we're talking

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.700
about contextual traces
for Cloud Logging, Cloud

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.830
certifications, and NEXT '21.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:07.670
I'm Carter Morgan.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.170
And welcome to "This
Week in Cloud,"

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.570
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.030
The need for relevant and
contextual telemetry data

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.150
to support online services
has grown in the last decade

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.060
as businesses undergo
digital transformation.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.220
Distributed tracing
is a key capability

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.010
for improving application
performance and reliability,

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.350
as noted in SRE best practices.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.000
Today, we're making
it easier for you

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.369
to understand what is happening
within your applications

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:35.310
by making trace information
available directly in Cloud

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:36.780
Logging.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.120
This past August,
50 service members

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.120
began a 12-week Google
Cloud-sponsored certification

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.400
learning journey towards
achieving the Google Cloud

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.250
Associate Cloud
Engineer certification.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.040
Participants had access to
online, on-demand learning

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.740
assets, biweekly
technical review sessions

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.810
taught by Google
engineers, and mentoring

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.070
through Google Groups.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.540
To learn more about
this initiative

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.610
to help upskill veterans
for an evolving job

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.040
market and the value of
Cloud certifications,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.570
check out the blog.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.940
If you missed the
fun from NEXT '21,

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.730
you're now able to check out
all that content on-demand.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.620
From keynotes to demos,
click on the link

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.060
to be a part of the action.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.020
What a year.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.050
As 2021 winds down,
we're preparing for 2022

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.450
by taking a deep breath and
looking back at all we've

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.037
accomplished since January.

00:01:20.037 --> 00:01:21.870
We hope you'll take the
next few weeks to do

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.200
what you can for yourself.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.507
And we'll see you in 2022
with the lowest latency news.

00:01:26.507 --> 00:01:28.590
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.820
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.010
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.640
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.140
We'll see you in the Cloud.

